diff --git a/docs/hermes-cache-acceptance.md b/docs/hermes-cache-acceptance.md
index c5da5af..19c46d0 100644
--- a/docs/hermes-cache-acceptance.md
+++ b/docs/hermes-cache-acceptance.md
@@ -56,6 +56,17 @@ disables root-disk loading AND storing - without it a warm disk would serve the
     DELETE dropping non-pinned tips only. Record peak host RAM and retained lines; the fork
     budget must hold at least depth+1 intended lines.
 
+7. F2b turn-boundary tips (CPU-verified; GPU acceptance pending): the tip's re-renderable point
+   sits at the LAST TURN BOUNDARY inside the prompt, not the raw prompt end. CPU probe with the
+   real tokenizer + pack template (case-3 bodies): parent1 raw n=11731, boundary L=11726 (5-token
+   generation-header tail), LCP(parent1, parent2)=11730; raw-n is a prefix of neither parent2 nor
+   the fork child, L is a prefix of both. Reproduce CPU-only with
+   `python tools/probe_turn_prefix.py --tokenizer <pack>/tokenizer --body
+   <bisect-body.json> [--rep N] [--assistant1 @file]`. Owner GPU rerun still pending: c3
+   parent2_after_child / parent3_after_fork must resume from the tip at ~len(parent prompt) with
+   suffix = the new messages only, fork_child must recall the planted password; token parity is
+   explicitly NOT a criterion (known-answer + deep-prefix recall instead).
+
 ## S2 cache API (GET/DELETE /v1/cache)
 
 Same auth as `/v1/models` (Bearer or x-api-key; 401 without a valid key when configured). GET and DELETE are supported; unknown GET/DELETE paths return 404.
